Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||04-15-2001||08:37 PM||||Since I am looking to buy a used car in the next month or so I registered with Carfax. I was seriously thinking of Buying a '88 Formula from ebay this morning (it went for $1025), but I ran the carFax check on the VIN number and it was only able to turn up one record on the car, that it was sold at auction last July with 104k miles on the odo. <P>  This didnt sit right with me, there was no records found of the car ever being titled, inspected, registered... nothing but that one auction sale. <P> Does this sound ligit? Do titles and registrations in some states not show up on CarFax? All the other cars i have been running CarFax checks on always turn up the original title and title transfer dates and locations. Is it possible this car has a fake VIN number?!<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||04-16-2001||09:12 AM||||Maybe I should ask the more general question: How much weight do you guys put on a CarFax report. If you find a really great looking deal (like the one I passed up on yesterday) but the CarFax report doesnt pass the smell test, would you pass up on the car?<P>What would you have to see in a CarFax report to make you let an otherwise good looking deal slip by?<P>I saw another car I was interested in this weekend, but I noticed that according to the CarFax report the car had gone from 40,000 miles or so to 60,000 miles in 21 days (according to the inspection and titling records), ie, it was driven 1000 miles a day for 20 days?! <P>Would you take that as a sign that something funny is going on with that car (someone transfered a VIN number from a wrecked car to a stolen one for example)? Would you pass up on a good deal based on that info?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||04-16-2001||09:14 AM||||BTW the CarFax report for that car didnt flag the 1000 mile per day for 3 weeks thing. It said the car history checks out "OK - no problems!"||||reg||1
